1.3.1 (2026-09-23)

- Improved: Much faster discovery of the Cast/UPnP bridge (DIAL server)
- Improved: DLNA (UPnP) renderers are pruned from the "Play To" target list automatically if they have not been seen on the network for 7 days (except for the configured default renderer)
- Fixed: The default_service setting, if set to "youtube", no longer reverts back to "auto" on each startup (only the first time after upgrading), allowing users to deliberately keep it set to "youtube" if they choose to

1.3.0 (2026-09-22)

- New: Introduced "Play To" feature to quickly play an online video to any DLNA (UPnP) renderer found on the network
- New: Introduced "Cast-to-UPnP Bridge" feature (DIAL server) to quickly play videos from compatible apps (e.g. the YouTube app) to any DLNA (UPnP) renderer found on the network
- New: Allow the resolving proxy modes and scheduled proactive resolving for Custom Playlists as well, enabling for locally-curated, multi-service "Watch Later" playlists
- New: Quick "Add to playlist" UI for Custom Playlists being used as local Watch Later lists (also allowing reordering and deleting items)
- New: If no Custom Playlists are present, the "Add to playlist" UI offers to quickly create your first "Custom Watch Later" playlist
- New: Added a "Quick Actions" panel to the dashboard overview page with buttons to commonly used procedures
- New: Introduced an "auto" service, allowing yt-dlp to choose the extractor automatically, which is the new default (automatically updated in configuration if not customized)
- New: Added no-remux proxy routes for explicitly disabling remuxing if otherwise enabled
- New: "View Playlist" page now shows more information, offers direct "Play to" links, and allows for deleting items
- Improved: Faster startup of ffmpeg remux process
- Improved: New default DASH format selector for YouTube, fixing URLs not being resolved on multi-language videos (automatically updated in configuration if not customized)
- Improved: The UDN UUID for the DLNA server is now auto-generated on first run instead of being hard-coded in dlna_server.py
- Improved: "View Playlist" is now implemented as a separate HTML asset instead of inside dashboard.py, making the code more maintainable
- Improved: Many improvements to Web UI, especially to mobile views
- Fixed: Using "View Playlist" on an empty Custom Playlist, immediately after creating it, returned HTTP 500

1.2.0 (2026-08-30)

- New: Custom sync intervals per playlist
- New: Time of last playlist sync is shown in Web UI now
- New: Command-line options and Web UI buttons to rebuild playlist library and purge CDN URL cache
- New: Command-line options --sync and --serve can be used together, forcing an initial sync of all playlists before launching the daemon
- New: Logs are visible in the Web UI with live update
- New: Added proxy routes for explicitly selecting remux target formats (/remux/mp4, /remux/ts)
- Improved: Logging now uses colors and has configurable verbosity (via configuration and command-line option)
- Improved: Optimized handling (caching) of the configuration file for minimized disk I/O
- Improved: Saving JSON files is done via a save-replace operation, avoiding conflicts with external processes writing to them
- Improved: Clearer wording in Web UI regarding settings inheritance for playlists
- Improved: Some more Web UI tweaks, like improved mobile views etc.
- Fixed: Wrong CDN URLs could get stored in cache if resolution previously had failed for one or more videos
- Fixed: Stale ffmpeg processes could remain in memory after client disconnects in TS mode

1.1.0 (2026-08-16)

- New: Introduced on-the-fly DASH remultiplexing via ffmpeg
- New: Added Web UI (dashboard and configuration interface) with light and dark mode
- New: Added Custom Playlists feature for hierarchical, locally-curated playlists
- New: Added more proxy routes to select specific modes independently from the default operating mode
- Improved: Optimized URL resolving performance by letting yt-dlp batch-resolve a collection of playlist items at once
- Improved: Optimized DLNA Server compatibility with more clients
- Improved: Configuration file is automatically created from example on first run
- Fixed: Fixed a possible race condition when updating URL cache file
- Fixed: Config file was not correctly interpreted as UTF-8 if running on Windows

1.0.0 (2026-08-03)

- Initial release to the public
